WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.719
The Aquaman movie is finally on its way to
being a real thing.

00:00:03.719 --> 00:00:08.210
The solo adventure for the DC Comics character
rolled out its first full trailer, and the

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:12.089
result has people feeling more excited than
they thought they could ever be over a superhero

00:00:12.089 --> 00:00:13.690
who can talk to fish.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:18.110
The movie's long-awaited first trailer provides
the clearest look yet at what we can expect

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.310
from the murky depths.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:24.090
Here are all the details you may have missed
from the first Aquaman movie trailer.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.490
The Trench

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:30.650
One of the trailer's most exciting shots involves
Jason Momoa's Aquaman and Amber Heard's Mera

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.760
diving into the ocean to escape a swarm of
monsters.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.660
This evil group chasing after the Atlantean
heroes are members of a society known as the

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:44.390
Trench, who were first introduced in a 2011
Aquaman comics run by writer Geoff Johns,

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.579
who has a story credit on the film.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:50.390
Formerly Atlanteans themselves, the Trench
are a splinter sect that was formed when the

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:55.769
legendary city sank into the sea, with their
group falling deep into the Marianas Trench.

00:00:55.769 --> 00:01:00.530
While the rest of the surviving Atlantis population
adapted to undersea life and maintained their

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:05.190
humanoid looks, the Trench became monstrous
and cannibalistic, adopting savage methods

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.580
of hunting and marauding in order to survive.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.500
Led by their own King and Queen, the Trench
serves as a dark mirror image to the other

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.830
prosperous Atlanteans, sea monsters who are
some of the more formidable dangers of the

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.010
deep.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.900
Vulko

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.640
One shot of the trailer lingers on a teenaged
Aquaman or an Aquateen, if you will training

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.340
in the art of catching a spear in between
his hands, a move he puts to good use as an

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.340
adult.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.210
That training sequence also offers a short
glimpse of Willem Dafoe's character, Vulko,

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:34.210
in action.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:39.660
According to Dafoe, Vulko is essentially Arthur's
mentor figure, being 100 percent Atlantean

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.890
while Arthur is half human and was raised
on the surface.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:47.600
They're characters with a lot of comics history
together, with Vulko serving as Arthur's regent

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.410
after he takes the Atlantean throne.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.770
Swim good

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:56.620
A big moment in the Aquaman trailer is his
explosive arrival on a submarine.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.820
"permission to come aboard."

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.050
But what you might have missed is Aquaman's
approach to the submarine.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:06.450
It only lasts about a second, and shows Aquaman
super-swimming his way toward the sub, a skill

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.909
we haven't really gotten to see him show off
in his earlier movie appearances.

00:02:09.909 --> 00:02:14.020
Regardless, it's a power he's long had in
the comics, being able to swim at the rate

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:17.200
of 6,800 miles per hour.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.569
Home invasion?

00:02:18.569 --> 00:02:22.740
The other big highlight of the trailer is
Black Manta, or if you're not a longtime comics

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.829
fan the guy in the evil SCUBA suit.

00:02:24.829 --> 00:02:28.890
Beyond having one of the coolest looks in
the entire history of comic book movies, it

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:32.489
looks like the Aquaman rival will play a part
in some deeply personal drama.

00:02:32.489 --> 00:02:37.420
In the Geoff Johns comics from which Aquaman
partially takes inspiration, Black Manta gets

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:42.860
hired by a doctor named Stephen Shin to acquire
a blood sample from Aquaman as a boy, in a

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:45.120
bid to prove that he's something more than
human.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.920
The pursuit ultimately results in the hero's
father's death.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:52.639
In the trailer, Black Manta is seen in full
combat mode in a domestic location.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:56.599
As the only surface-side household we see
in the trailer, it's tempting to think that

00:02:56.599 --> 00:03:01.389
this set piece takes place inside of the lighthouse
home of Aquaman's childhood, which would spell

00:03:01.389 --> 00:03:06.341
pretty terrible things for the one non-superpowered
member of his family should Black Manta get

00:03:06.341 --> 00:03:08.239
his hands on him.

00:03:08.239 --> 00:03:09.379
Unite the Seven

00:03:09.379 --> 00:03:13.189
In addition to giving audiences an idea of
what they're in for on their journey under

00:03:13.189 --> 00:03:17.989
the sea with Aquaman and friends, the Aquaman
trailer finally gave moviegoers an answer

00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:20.620
to a question that's been lingering out there
for years.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:25.090
Specifically, after all this time, we finally
know the meaning of the phrase "Unite the

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:26.090
Seven."

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:30.540
The very first image of Jason Momoa's Aquaman
came in February 2015, more than three years

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.500
before his solo movie's release date.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.499
That image was superimposed with the phrase
"Unite the Seven."

00:03:35.499 --> 00:03:39.700
At the time, and for years after, no one was
really certain what this phrase was meant

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:40.700
to convey.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:44.790
As it turns out, the tagline refers to what
appears to be the general plot of Aquaman,

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:49.090
with Arthur's half-brother Orm working to
unite the seven kingdoms of the ocean into

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:52.790
one unified force to take on the surface world
in all-out war.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:56.860
"And I'm bringing the wrath of the seven seas
with me."

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:57.860
Just talk

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:02.379
Another aspect of undersea living that a lot
of people don't think about is communication.

00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:06.750
Justice League had Mera use her control over
water to create an air bubble for the purposes

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:07.849
of conversation.

00:04:07.849 --> 00:04:12.980
Luckily, that weird, potentially drama-crippling
solution isn't being brought over to Aquaman's

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.000
solo outing.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.950
Director James Wan confirmed
as much on Twitter, writing, "Fret not, no

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.560
'air bubbles for dialogue' in my underwater
world."

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.229
So how do they talk underwater in Aquaman?

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:26.840
The answer, as the trailer confirms, is that
they just can.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:28.980
Sometimes it's best not to overthink things.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:32.190
"That was the worst pep talk ever.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:33.280
Nereus

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.500
The trailer for Aquaman sets up a lot about
the movie, even though it doesn't linger too

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.479
long on everything it introduces.

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:43.900
One of those quick glimpses appears to introduce
Dolph Lundgren's character Nereus.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:47.300
We don't know much about what Nereus will
get up to in this movie, but we do know that

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:51.630
he's been substantially altered from his comic
book counterpart in at least one way.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:56.330
In the comics, he and Mera were in a relationship
in the movie, they're evidently father and

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.840
daughter.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.479
Yellow eyes

00:04:59.479 --> 00:05:03.850
As played by Jason Momoa, the Aquaman of the
movies has typically been shown as having

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.680
some mystically pale eyes.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:09.820
But one pivotal moment in the Aquaman trailer
appears to be a whole new invention for the

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:13.659
character the yellow shade that young Arthur's
eyes turn as he communicates with the sea

00:05:13.659 --> 00:05:14.660
life in the aquarium.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.409
It'd be understandable to think that those
yellow eyes come straight from the comic books,

00:05:18.409 --> 00:05:20.819
but that doesn't seem to be the case.

00:05:20.819 --> 00:05:24.780
Most likely, it's a movie invention meant
solely for the audience to understand when

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:27.570
Arthur's revving up to throw a pile of sharks
at his enemies.

